# Fallback mirror for the mesa release tarball, read by ./fetch-source.sh (the one fetch for both
# packages/mesa and packages/mesa-x86).
#
# Fedora's lookaside serves the pristine upstream tarball (byte-identical, checked for 26.2.1) from
# a host independent of freedesktop. archive.mesa3d.org is a single machine, and
# mesa.freedesktop.org fills from the same origin, so both go down together (both were unreachable
# for over half an hour on 2026-08-23). Debian repacks mesa, Gentoo's distfiles lacked 26.2.1, and
# sources.archlinux.org does not rehost it.
#
# The mirror is not trusted: fetch-source.sh checks whatever it gets against the sha256 in
# ./PKGBUILD and fails on a mismatch. So it can only make a build succeed that would otherwise
# fail, never change what is built.
#
# This is a separate file, not a field of ./source.pin, because packages/inputhash.sh hashes
# source.pin into rootfs/manifest.lock: refreshing the mirror should cost neither a relock nor a
# mesa rebuild.
#
#   sha512  the tarball's SHA512, used only to build the lookaside URL (Fedora puts it in the
#           path); not an integrity check. On a bump, read it from
#             https://src.fedoraproject.org/repo/pkgs/mesa/mesa-<ver>.tar.xz/sha512/
#           and leave it empty if Fedora has not packaged that version yet: fetch-source.sh then
#           tries upstream only. A wrong value costs a 404 on the fallback, never a wrong build.
sha512: 0959679a8e9560a36d63bfc67357c73fde6fd98b00c29859ab30b31454b9ef8c8def38c7e180b168fd39080681042559dfc4a4252dfb289930a9776e0243c2dc
